course: dictionary
lesson: 11306
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word year can mean a time of 365 days, a class at school, or a long time. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: «Chloe and Bella are still frenemies in Year 6» uses Year with a number, so it means a school class, not a length of time. «I haven't seen her for years» uses years to mean a long time, because it tells you how long it has been.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Is it about the Earth going round the sun, school, or a long stretch of time? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A year is the time the Earth takes to go once around the sun.
fact: A year has 12 months, 52 weeks or 365 days.
fact: A leap year has 366 days.
fact: «Year 4» means a class at school, used in the UK, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Years» can mean a long time, as in «I haven't seen her for years».
exercise: What is a year? The time the Earth takes to go once around what? | Star | Moon | Mars | *Sun
exercise: «Chloe and Bella are still frenemies in Year 6.» What does Year 6 mean? | *A school class | A long time | A time of 365 days | A leap year
exercise: «I haven't seen her for years.» What does years mean? | Twelve months | Exactly 365 days | *A long time | Only once
test: How many days does a leap year have? | *366 | 52 | 12 | 365
test: In «scientists bred only the tamest foxes for over 60 years», which meaning of years fits? | *A long span of time | A leap year of 366 days | A school class | A single day
exam: Which meaning of year does «Year 6» show, a school class or a long time? | A leap year | A long time | The time the Earth takes to go round the sun | *A school class
